cff-version: 1.2.0
message: >-
  If you use this software, please cite the dissertation below, and the
  article behind the test you use (listed under references).
title: "fdachange: Epidemic Change-Point Tests for Functional Data"
type: software
authors:
  - family-names: Bartkus
    given-names: Karolis
    orcid: "https://orcid.org/0009-0003-6476-8721"
version: 1.0.0
license: MIT
repository-code: "https://github.com/karbar359/fdachange"
abstract: >-
  Weighted scan tests for epidemic (changed-segment) alternatives in scalar
  and functional data: an antisymmetric-kernel (Wilcoxon-type) scan, an
  Lp-type scan of the weighted empirical process, a kernel mean-embedding
  (RKHS) scan, and the CUSUM-type statistic of Birbilas (2025), with
  precomputed Monte-Carlo critical values, functional-to-scalar projections
  and curve reconstruction. R package with a Python twin.
keywords:
  - change-point detection
  - epidemic alternative
  - functional data analysis
  - scan statistics
  - R
  - Python
